        "starter_html": "<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Task Tracker</title>\n<h1>Task Tracker</h1>\n<form id=\"form\">\n  <label for=\"title\">New task</label>\n  <input id=\"title\" required maxlength=\"160\">\n  <button type=\"submit\">Add task</button>\n</form>\n<ul id=\"tasks\"></ul>\n<script>\n// Implement the application below. This starter contains NO behavior.\n// Use one array loaded from localStorage.getItem('tasks') or [].\n// persist(): save the array to localStorage and call render().\n// render(): replace children of #tasks only, never the form or body.\n// For each task, create li, input checkbox, span with textContent, Delete button.\n// Checkbox change: update task.done and persist().\n// Delete click: remove the task by unique id from the global array and persist().\n// Form submit: preventDefault, trim #title, append {id,title,done:false}, clear,\n// and persist(). Use stable unique IDs and ignore empty strings.\n// Call render() once on page load. All state changes must persist after reload.\n</script>\n</html>\n",
        "starter_instruction": "Complete the missing JavaScript in this explicit starter. Preserve its form and tasks list. No CSS or extra features are needed. Return the complete HTML file.",
        "constraints": "No dependencies, network calls, remote assets, or backend. Add task via labeled input and Add task button, checkbox complete, Delete button, localStorage persistence. Use textContent for user input. The textbox MUST have an actual label element with matching for/id, or aria-label; placeholder alone is NOT accessible. Render task titles in their own span. Use stable unique task ids. Keep one global tasks array; render() should take no arguments so deletion cannot shadow the global state. Persist after each change."
      },
